    <statement><p>Find the derivative of the function <m>q(r)</m>, below.  It may be to your
advantage to simplify  first.</p>
<p><me>\displaystyle q(r)={2 r\over 4 r + 8}</me></p>
<p><m>q'(r) =</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{2\mathopen{}\left(4r+8\right)-2\cdot 4r}{\left(4r+8\right)^{2}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>SOLUTION</p>
<p><me>q'(r) = \frac{2 (4 r + 8) - 8 r}{(4 r + 8)^2} 
         = \frac{16}{(4 r + 8)^2}.</me></p>
</solution>
